#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:1
msgid "FlagOS Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:3
msgid ""
"FlagOS is a fully open-source AI system software stack for heterogeneous "
"AI chips, allowing AI models to be developed once and seamlessly ported "
"to a wide range of AI hardware with minimal effort."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:6
#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:10
msgid "FlagOS architecture"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:8
msgid ""
"The figure below shows the position of FlagOS in the AI ecosystem and its"
" composition modules."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:10
msgid "![FlagOS architecture](images/flagos-architecture-en.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:12
msgid ""
"FlagOS 2.2 comprises the following core libraries, plugins, domain-"
"specific projects, developer tools, and platform services."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:14
msgid "Open-source core libraries"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:16
msgid "Operator libraries"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:17
msgid "**General-purpose operator library**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:18
msgid "**FlagGems** (v5.4.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:20
msgid ""
"FlagGems is a high-performance general-purpose operator library "
"implemented with the Triton programming language and its extended "
"languages. FlagGems is designed to provide a suite of general-purpose "
"operators for large models, accelerating the inference and training of "
"models across multiple backend platforms."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:22
msgid "**Fused operator libraries**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:23
msgid "**FlagGems-vllm** (v0.2.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:25
msgid ""
"A high-performance operator library designed for multiple hardware "
"backends. It provides optimized implementations of common vLLM operators "
"and supports high-performance inference and deployment for a variety of "
"widely used models."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:27
msgid "**FlagGems-sglang** (v0.1.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:29
msgid ""
"A high-performance multi-backend operator library for SGLang inference "
"workflows. Implemented with Triton, it provides optimized implementations"
" of common SGLang operators for efficient model deployment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:31
msgid "**Multi-domain operator libraries**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:33
msgid "**FlagDNN** (v0.3.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:35
msgid ""
"A deep neural network computing library oriented towards multiple chip "
"backends. It provides high-performance implementations of common deep "
"learning operators."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:37
msgid "**FlagBLAS** (v0.3.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:39
msgid ""
"A computing library that follows the BLAS standard interface and is "
"oriented towards multiple chip backends. It defines core operations for "
"numerical calculations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:41
msgid "**FlagFFT** (v0.2.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:43
msgid ""
"A JIT-compiled GPU FFT library. It generates CUDA kernels at runtime via "
"Triton/TLE and libtriton_jit, targeting arbitrary-length transforms that "
"cuFFT does not optimally support."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:45
msgid "**FlagSparse** (v0.3.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:47
msgid ""
"A domain-specific operator library that contains operators dedicated to "
"sparse computation scenarios."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:49
msgid "**FlagTensor** (v0.3.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:51
msgid ""
"A high-performance tensor-primitive library implemented in Triton "
"language. It provides optimized implementations of common tensor "
"primitives (unary, binary, and tensor contraction operations) benchmarked"
" against cuTensor baselines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:53
msgid "**FlagAttention** (v0.4.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:55
msgid ""
"FlagAttention is a collection of memory-efficient attention operators "
"implemented in Triton for training and inference workloads. It supports "
"dense attention, paged or sparse KV-cache layouts, recurrent linear "
"attention, and multiple hardware backends."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:57
msgid "**FlagAudio** (v0.2.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:59
msgid ""
"A multi-backend computing library that adheres to Audio standard "
"interfaces. It delivers a high-performance computing solution designed "
"for audio signal processing and speech AI applications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:61
msgid ""
"**FlagTree** (GPU: `0.7.0+triton3.6` / `0.7.0+triton3.5` / "
"`0.7.0+triton3.3`; CPU: `v0.1.0`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:63
msgid ""
"FlagTree is an open-source, unified compiler for multiple AI chips. "
"FlagTree is dedicated to building a compiler and associated tooling "
"platform for diverse AI chips, advancing and expanding the upstream and "
"downstream Triton ecosystem, with the goals of supporting existing "
"adaptation solutions, unifying code repositories, and enabling rapid "
"multi-backend support from a single repository. For upstream model users,"
" FlagTree provides unified compilation support across multiple backends; "
"for downstream chip vendors, FlagTree offers reference implementations "
"for integration into the Triton ecosystem."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:65
msgid "**FlagScale** (v2.1.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:67
msgid ""
"FlagScale is a comprehensive toolkit designed to support the entire "
"lifecycle of large models. FlagScale builds on the strengths of several "
"prominent open-source projects, including Megatron-LM and vLLM, to "
"provide a robust, end-to-end solution for managing and scaling large "
"models."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:69
msgid "**FlagCX** (v0.14.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:71
msgid ""
"FlagCX is a scalable and adaptive unified communication library for "
"cross-chip environments. FlagCX delivers high-performance point-to-point "
"and collective communication capabilities tailored for multi-chip, multi-"
"platform scenarios. By leveraging the native collective communication "
"capabilities of each platform, FlagCX incorporates technologies such as "
"device-buffer IPC and RDMA to enable highly efficient collective "
"communication in both cross-chip and single-chip scenarios, while also "
"providing adaptive tuning capabilities for communication optimization."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:73
msgid "Plugins"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:75
msgid ""
"The FlagOS ecosystem enablement layer adopts a plugin architecture "
"composed of the following modules. Each module bridges an upstream "
"library and its backend engine with the FlagOS core libraries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:77
msgid "**vllm-plugin-FL**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:79
msgid ""
"vllm-plugin-FL extends the inference capabilities of vLLM to diverse AI "
"chips, enabling efficient model serving beyond the original supported "
"hardware. Built on FlagOS's unified multi-chip backend. The FlagOS 2.2 "
"release provides `v0.3.0` for the vLLM 0.24.0 line and `v0.2.2` for the "
"vLLM 0.20.2 line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:81
msgid "**sglang-plugin-FL** (v0.2.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:83
msgid ""
"sglang-plugin-FL is an out-of-tree (OOT) plugin for SGLang, built on "
"FlagOS's unified multi-chip backend. It extends SGLang's inference "
"capabilities across diverse hardware platforms."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:85
msgid "**Torch-FL** (v2.10.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:87
msgid ""
"Torch-FL is a custom PyTorch device plugin based on the PrivateUse1 "
"extension mechanism. It registers FlagGems high-performance Triton "
"operators, vendor-native operator libraries, and CUDA compatibility "
"kernels behind one `flagos` device name, providing a unified runtime and "
"operator-routing layer across diverse AI chips."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:89
msgid "**Megatron-LM-FL** (v0.3.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:91
msgid ""
"Megatron-LM-FL extends the distributed training capabilities of Megatron-"
"LM to diverse AI chips, supporting scalable large-model training across "
"heterogeneous hardware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:93
msgid "**TransformerEngine-FL** (v0.3.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:95
msgid ""
"TransformerEngine-FL extends the transformer acceleration capabilities of"
" Transformer Engine to diverse AI chips, enabling hardware-agnostic "
"training acceleration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:97
msgid "**verl-FL** (v0.2.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:99
msgid ""
"verl-FL extends the reinforcement learning capabilities of veRL to "
"diverse AI chips, broadening the hardware coverage for RL-based training "
"workflows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:101
msgid ""
"vllm-plugin-FL, Megatron-LM-FL, TransformerEngine-FL, and verl-FL can be "
"used together with FlagScale. When only one or two capabilities are "
"required — such as training, inference, or reinforcement learning — the "
"corresponding module can independently bridge its upstream library and "
"backend engine with the relevant FlagOS core library modules, offering "
"the flexibility to meet diverse user deployment scenarios."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:103
msgid "Domain-specific projects"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:105
msgid "**FlagOS-Robo** (v0.1.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:107
msgid ""
"FlagOS-Robo is a chip-agnostic framework for training and deploying "
"Vision Language Models (VLMs) and Vision Language Action (VLA) models "
"across edge-to-cloud scenarios in Embodied Intelligence. It treats VLMs "
"as the \"brain\" for task planning and VLA models as the \"cerebellum\" "
"for generating robot control actions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:109
msgid "**FlagQuantum** (v0.1.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:111
msgid ""
"FlagQuantum is a high-performance distributed quantum statevector "
"simulator built on PyTorch, enabling quantum circuit simulation across "
"multiple GPUs with automatic sharding and resharding."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:113
msgid "Developer tools"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:115
msgid "**KernelGen** (v2.2.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:117
msgid ""
"KernelGen is an operator auto-generation tool. KernelGen is designed to "
"construct operator definitions through natural language prompts, retrieve"
" existing similar operator definitions, automatically execute operator "
"accuracy and performance testing, generate accuracy and performance test "
"results, and produce Triton Kernels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:119
msgid "**FlagOS-Compressor** (v0.1.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:121
msgid ""
"FlagOS-Compressor is a checkpoint conversion and quantization tool for "
"local Hugging Face `safetensors` model directories. It supports "
"quantizing model weights, converting checkpoints, calibrating outputs, "
"and validating generated artifacts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:123
msgid "**FlagOS Skills** (v1.1.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:125
msgid ""
"FlagOS Skills are agent-compatible capabilities designed to streamline "
"key FlagOS workflows, including deployment, operator development, "
"migration, adoption, and performance evaluation. Compatible with Claude "
"Code, Cursor, Codex, and any agent supporting the Agent Skills standard."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:127
msgid "**Online Laboratory**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:129
msgid ""
"An online laboratory providing cloud-based development environments for "
"FlagOS projects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:131
msgid "Platform services"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:133
msgid "**FlagRelease** (v0.1.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:135
msgid ""
"FlagRelease is a platform dedicated to the automatic migration, "
"adaptation and release of large models for multi-architecture AI chips. "
"FlagRelease aims to enable mainstream large models to be migrated, "
"validated, and released on diverse domestic AI hardware with lower cost "
"and higher efficiency through automated, standardized, and intelligent "
"adaptation workflows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:137
msgid "**FlagPerf** (v1.2.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:139
msgid ""
"FlagPerf is an integrated AI hardware evaluation engine. FlagPerf aims to"
" establish an industry practice-oriented indicator system and evaluate "
"the actual performance of AI hardware under combinations of software "
"stacks (model + framework + compiler)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:141
msgid "**FlagCICD** (v0.1.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:143
msgid ""
"FlagCICD is a CI/CD toolchain that streamlines large-model development "
"across diverse AI chips, eliminating fragmentation and cutting adaptation"
" costs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:145
msgid "**KernelGenBench** (v0.2.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../flagos_homepage/overview.md:147
msgid ""
"KernelGenBench is a benchmark framework for evaluating LLM and agent-"
"based Triton kernel generation across multiple hardware platforms."
msgstr ""

